---
// Berlin, restyled as a room. Rebuilt from Eduardo's own concept (a
// full redesign he sent over, already built against the site's real
// RoomNerve/RoomShell component CSS -- the structural CSS below is
// his, carried over verbatim; a stray Perplexity browser-extension
// script that had gotten baked into one export of it was stripped
// before any of this was used).
//
// "Sealed" vs "open" is decided client-side, against the real talk
// date, not at build time: the film and script ship in this page
// always, and a small script below toggles which state is shown.
// Worth being honest about what that does and doesn't protect: the
// video file already lives as a public, fetchable URL on the server
// (Eduardo uploaded it directly, before this page existed), and the
// full script text sits in this page's HTML regardless of the seal,
// hidden by CSS only. So the seal is a presentation choice for a
// casual visitor before 26 October, not an access control -- there
// is no real embargo left to protect technically. A ?sealed query
// param forces the pre-talk view for preview/testing either way.
//
// Opening moment: Monday 26 October 2026, 10:00 Berlin time (CET),
// from src/data/berlin.ts. The site is static (IONOS), so two things
// carry the opening:
// - At build time, `open` decides the noindex. A build made before
//   10:00 CET keeps noindex; the scheduled IONOS deploy at 09:00 UTC on
//   the 26th (.github/workflows/deploy-ionos.yml) rebuilds after the
//   moment, so the noindex disappears. BERLIN_OPEN=1 forces it open.
// - In the browser, the seal below uses the same BERLIN_OPENS and
//   reloads the page when the countdown reaches zero, as a backup if
//   the scheduled deploy is late.
import '../../styles/fraunces.css';
import '@fontsource/ibm-plex-mono/400.css';
import '@fontsource-variable/newsreader/opsz.css';
import '../../styles/global.css';
import RoomNerve from '../../components/RoomNerve.astro';
import RoomShell from '../../components/RoomShell.astro';
import { BERLIN_OPENS, berlinOpen } from '../../data/berlin';

const open = process.env.BERLIN_OPEN === '1' || berlinOpen();

const canonicalUrl = new URL('/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/', Astro.site);
const ogImageUrl = new URL('/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/film-poster.jpg', Astro.site);

// Both live only on the server (uploaded directly, not committed --
// see the deploy-ionos.yml notes on why large media stays out of
// git). The PDF hasn't been uploaded yet as of this page going in;
// the link will 404 until it is.
const VIDEO_SRC = '/automa-2026/AUTOMA-Chem-2026-web-animation%20.mp4';
const SCRIPT_PDF = '/automa-2026/AUTOMA-Chem-2026-Speaking-Script.pdf';

// Read directly from the film: the act numeral appears on screen at
// each of these seconds.
const CHAPTERS = [
  { n: '00', t: 'Title', at: 0 },
  { n: '01', t: 'The Architect', at: 52 },
  { n: '02', t: 'Brasília', at: 111 },
  { n: '03', t: 'Ambition becomes evidence', at: 187 },
  { n: '04', t: 'AI scales what is there', at: 255 },
  { n: '05', t: 'Digital twins', at: 321 },
  { n: '06', t: 'Close', at: 408 },
];
const DURATION = 467.3;

// Each act's body in the exact order it was spoken -- 'said' is the
// line pulled out as a quote, 'p' is running text. Eduardo's own
// script, unedited.
const acts = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'The Architect',
    seek: 52,
    body: [
      { p: 'I am an architect. Not as a metaphor. I studied architecture, I drew buildings, and then I spent the last twenty years designing something less visible: data and AI governance.' },
      { p: 'I work inside a chemical company, like many of you, and I have got plenty of these things wrong myself. But I keep seeing the same problem:' },
      { said: 'we design from above, not always for the person who has to live with the result.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Brasília',
    seek: 111,
    body: [
      { p: 'Let me take you to Brasília. From the air, it is extraordinary: monumental, precise, unforgettable. But at street level, it can feel very different. The scale is vast. The distances are large.' },
      { said: 'A city can make perfect sense from a helicopter and feel completely different when you walk through it.' },
      { p: 'We build governance in a similar way. We have policies, controls, committees, operating models, and occasionally, a beautiful RACI that makes everyone feel civilisation has finally arrived.' },
      { p: 'For about ten minutes. Then someone asks who is actually accountable.' },
      { p: 'Then the framework reaches the plant.' },
      { p: 'I have been the person with the beautiful drawing. I have presented the framework, watched people nod, and then watched them carry on exactly as before. They were not being difficult. I had built them a plaza nobody wanted to stand in.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Ambition becomes evidence',
    seek: 187,
    body: [
      { p: 'That matters when we talk about sustainable digital transformation. We set ambitions, targets and roadmaps. We invest in systems, automation and AI. But eventually, ambition has to become evidence.' },
      { said: 'A carbon number looks like chemistry. It is a data product.' },
      { p: 'Behind one apparently simple number sit supplier declarations, energy data, production records, transport data, allocation rules and assumptions. Much of it comes from systems that were never designed to agree with one another.' },
      { p: 'So the challenge is not simply calculating the number. The challenge is being able to explain it. Where did it come from? Who owns it? What definition sits behind it? And who is prepared to stand behind it when someone asks a difficult question?' },
      { p: 'You cannot report what you cannot trace.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'AI scales what is there',
    seek: 255,
    body: [
      { p: 'Then, inevitably, someone says: “Why do we not just use AI?”' },
      { p: 'I am optimistic about AI.' },
      { said: 'But AI does not remove ambiguity. It can scale it.' },
      { p: 'If five people use the word “batch” to mean five different things, putting an AI agent on top does not make the organisation clearer. It just gives the confusion a faster processor.' },
      { p: 'Sometimes AI is the answer. Sometimes the answer is better data. Sometimes it is a better process. And occasionally it is simply agreeing on what a word means before we ask a machine to interpret it.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '05',
    title: 'AI digital twins and smarter decisions',
    seek: 321,
    body: [
      { p: 'And take an AI digital twin.' },
      { p: 'It learns from the data of a real process: how equipment behaves, how materials respond, where energy is used, and where defects or waste occur.' },
      { p: 'Then it can help answer complex operational questions much faster. What if we change the temperature, the timing, or the material mix? Which settings could maintain quality while using less energy or producing less scrap?' },
      { p: 'Instead of relying on repeated physical trials, teams can use the AI digital twin to explore and compare possible outcomes before acting on the real process.' },
      { p: 'That can mean fewer wasted materials, less rework, and faster decisions about how to improve production.' },
      { said: 'This is one way AI can make sustainability practical: helping people find better ways to run the systems they already have, with less waste built in.' },
    ],
  },
  {
    n: '06',
    title: 'Close',
    seek: 408,
    body: [
      { p: 'So I want to leave you with one question.' },
      { p: 'What is one word in your organisation that means something different depending on which floor you are standing on?' },
      { p: 'Ask it at lunch. You may discover that the answer tells you more about your governance than another hundred pages of framework ever could.' },
      { p: 'Agents do not own risk. They do not carry accountability.' },
      { said: 'Humans do. Always.' },
    ],
  },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Berlin · Out Loud · EDUARDO sopalda</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation. From Brasília to the plant floor. AUTOMA Chem 2026, Estrel Berlin, 26 October 2026: the film and the script." />
    {!open && <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />}
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonicalUrl} />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Out loud · Berlin" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="A plan can be right from above and still fail the person who has to walk it. That distance is the talk." />
    <meta property="og:image" content={ogImageUrl} />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#000000" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <RoomNerve current="/out-loud" heading={false} />
    <RoomShell title="Out loud" italic="Berlin.">
      <ol class="acts-index" aria-label="The six acts" slot="rail-extra">
        {CHAPTERS.slice(1).map((c) => (
          <li data-act={c.n}>
            <button type="button" data-seek={c.at}>
              <span class="n">{c.n}</span>
              <span class="t">{c.t}</span>
              <span class="tc">{Math.floor(c.at / 60)}:{String(c.at % 60).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            </button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <p class="ol-kicker">AUTOMA Chem 2026 · Estrel Berlin · 26 October · 9:40</p>
      <h2 class="ol-title">Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation</h2>
      <p class="ol-deck">From Brasília to the plant floor.</p>
      <p class="ol-lede">A plan can be right from above and still fail the person who has to walk it. That distance is the talk.</p>

      <!-- ── the film ── -->
      <figure class="film" id="film" aria-label="The film of the talk">
        <div class="screen" id="screen" tabindex="0" role="button" aria-label="Play the film">
          <img class="poster" src="/out-loud/automa-chem-2026/film-poster.jpg" alt="Title card: Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation, Eduardo Sopalda" width="1280" height="720" />
          <video id="video" playsinline preload="none" data-src={VIDEO_SRC} aria-label="Data and AI in Sustainable Digital Transformation, film, 7 minutes 47"></video>
          <div class="cue-play" aria-hidden="true"><i class="cl"></i><i class="cd"></i><span>Play the film</span></div>
          <p class="now" id="now" aria-live="polite">00 · Title</p>
          <div class="seal" role="note">
            <span class="k">Sealed</span>
            <p class="l">The film and the script stay closed <em>until after the talk is given.</em></p>
            <span class="count" id="count">26 October · 10:00 CET</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="film-nerve" id="nerve" role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-label="Position in the film" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax={Math.round(DURATION)} aria-valuenow="0" aria-valuetext="0:00, Title">
          <div class="fn-track"></div>
          <div class="fn-fill" id="fill"></div>
          <div class="fn-head" id="head"></div>
          <!-- stops are placed by script from CHAPTERS -->
          <span class="fn-tip" id="tip"></span>
        </div>

        <figcaption class="film-bar">
          <button type="button" id="toggle">Play</button>
          <span class="time" id="time">0:00 / 7:47</span>
          <button type="button" id="full">Full screen</button>
          <span class="note">Silent, apart from one paper tap. The words are below.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- ── the script ── -->
      <section class="script" aria-labelledby="script-h">
        <div class="section-head">
          <h2 id="script-h">The script</h2>
          <p>Six acts · <a href={SCRIPT_PDF} data-open-only>PDF, two pages</a></p>
        </div>

        {acts.map((act) => (
          <article class="act" id={`act-${act.n}`} data-act={act.n}>
            <span class="act-n">{act.n}</span>
            <div>
              <h3>{act.title}</h3>
              <button type="button" class="watch" data-seek={act.seek}>Watch from {Math.floor(act.seek / 60)}:{String(act.seek % 60).padStart(2, '0')}</button>
              <p class="closed">Closed until after the talk.</p>
              <div class="body">
                {act.body.map((item) => (
                  'said' in item
                    ? <span class="said">{item.said}</span>
                    : <p>{item.p}</p>
                ))}
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        ))}
      </section>

      <!-- ── the question left in the room ── -->
      <section class="question" aria-labelledby="q-k">
        <p class="ol-kicker" id="q-k">The question I left in the room</p>
        <p class="q">What is one word in your organisation that means something different depending on which floor you are standing on?</p>
        <p class="after">I asked it in Berlin. Now I am asking you.</p>
        <p class="links"><a href="/contact">Send me your word</a></p>
      </section>

      <dl class="colophon">
        <div><dt>Event</dt><dd>AUTOMA Chem 2026</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Room</dt><dd>Estrel Berlin<br />26 October 2026 · 9:40</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Speaker</dt><dd>Eduardo Sopalda<br />D&amp;T Global Data Governance Lead, <span class="brand-name" style="white-space:nowrap">dsm-firmenich</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Film</dt><dd>7:47 · six acts<br />silent, one paper tap</dd></div>
      </dl>

      <p class="back"><a href="/out-loud">← Out loud</a></p>
    </RoomShell>

    <script define:vars={{ chapters: CHAPTERS, duration: DURATION, opens: BERLIN_OPENS }}>
      /* Out Loud · Berlin — film, nerve and script, one clock. */
      const CHAPTERS = chapters;
      const DURATION = duration;
      // The film opens after the talk: 26 Oct 2026, 10:00 in Berlin (CET, UTC+1).
      // Same moment as BERLIN_OPENS in src/data/berlin.ts.
      const OPENS = opens;

      const $ = (s, r = document) => r.querySelector(s);
      const $$ = (s, r = document) => [...r.querySelectorAll(s)];
      const body = document.body;
      const film = $('#film'), screen = $('#screen'), video = $('#video');
      const nerve = $('#nerve'), fill = $('#fill'), head = $('#head'), tip = $('#tip');
      const toggle = $('#toggle'), time = $('#time'), now = $('#now');
      const reduce = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

      /* seal ─ ?open / ?sealed override the clock for previews */
      const q = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
      const sealed = Date.now() < OPENS && !q.has('open') || q.has('sealed');
      body.dataset.seal = sealed ? 'sealed' : 'open';
      $$('[data-open-only]').forEach(a => { if (sealed) { a.removeAttribute('href'); a.setAttribute('aria-disabled', 'true'); a.style.opacity = .4; } });
      if (sealed) {
        screen.removeAttribute('role'); screen.removeAttribute('tabindex');
        const tick = () => {
          const ms = Math.max(0, OPENS - Date.now());
          // Backup reveal: when the moment arrives on an open tab, reload
          // so the page comes back unsealed (unless ?sealed forces it).
          if (ms === 0 && !q.has('sealed')) { location.reload(); return; }
          const d = Math.floor(ms / 864e5), h = Math.floor(ms / 36e5) % 24, m = Math.floor(ms / 6e4) % 60;
          $('#count').textContent = `Opens in ${d} d · ${String(h).padStart(2,'0')} h · ${String(m).padStart(2,'0')} m`;
        };
        tick(); setInterval(tick, 30e3);
      }

      /* stops on the film's nerve */
      CHAPTERS.forEach((c, i) => {
        const b = document.createElement('button');
        b.type = 'button'; b.className = 'fn-stop'; b.dataset.i = i;
        b.style.left = (c.at / DURATION * 100) + '%';
        b.setAttribute('aria-label', `${c.n} ${c.t}, ${fmt(c.at)}`);
        b.innerHTML = `<b>${c.n}</b><i></i>`;
        b.addEventListener('click', e => { e.stopPropagation(); seek(c.at, true); });
        b.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => showTip(c.at, `${c.n} · ${c.t}`));
        nerve.insertBefore(b, tip);
      });
      const stops = $$('.fn-stop');

      function fmt(s) { s = Math.max(0, Math.floor(s)); return `${Math.floor(s / 60)}:${String(s % 60).padStart(2, '0')}`; }
      function chapterAt(s) { let i = 0; CHAPTERS.forEach((c, k) => { if (s >= c.at) i = k; }); return i; }
      function showTip(s, label) { tip.style.left = (s / DURATION * 100) + '%'; tip.textContent = label; }

      function load() {
        if (!video.src) { video.src = video.dataset.src; video.preload = 'auto'; }
      }
      function play() { if (sealed) return; load(); film.dataset.started = '1'; video.play().catch(() => {}); }
      function pause() { video.pause(); }
      function seek(s, andPlay) {
        if (sealed) return;
        load(); film.dataset.started = '1';
        const go = () => { video.currentTime = Math.min(s + 0.05, DURATION - .1); if (andPlay) video.play().catch(() => {}); render(s); };
        video.readyState >= 1 ? go() : video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', go, { once: true });
      }

      let lastActive = -1;
      function render(s = video.currentTime || 0) {
        const p = Math.min(1, s / DURATION) * 100;
        fill.style.width = p + '%';
        head.style.left = p + '%';
        time.textContent = `${fmt(s)} / ${fmt(DURATION)}`;
        const i = chapterAt(s);
        stops.forEach((b, k) => { b.dataset.passed = s >= CHAPTERS[k].at ? '1' : '0'; b.dataset.active = k === i ? '1' : '0'; });
        nerve.setAttribute('aria-valuenow', Math.floor(s));
        nerve.setAttribute('aria-valuetext', `${fmt(s)}, ${CHAPTERS[i].t}`);
        if (i !== lastActive) {
          lastActive = i;
          now.textContent = `${CHAPTERS[i].n} · ${CHAPTERS[i].t}`;
          $$('.act, .acts-index li').forEach(el => { el.dataset.active = (el.dataset.act === CHAPTERS[i].n) ? '1' : '0'; });
        }
        body.dataset.following = (film.dataset.playing === '1' && i >= 1) ? '1' : '0';
      }

      video.addEventListener('timeupdate', () => render());
      video.addEventListener('play', () => { film.dataset.playing = '1'; render(); toggle.textContent = 'Pause'; screen.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Pause the film'); });
      video.addEventListener('pause', () => { film.dataset.playing = '0'; render(); toggle.textContent = 'Play'; screen.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Play the film'); });
      video.addEventListener('ended', () => { body.dataset.following = '0'; toggle.textContent = 'Again'; });

      const flip = () => (video.paused ? play() : pause());
      screen.addEventListener('click', flip);
      screen.addEventListener('keydown', e => { if (e.key === ' ' || e.key === 'Enter') { e.preventDefault(); flip(); } });
      toggle.addEventListener('click', flip);
      $('#full').addEventListener('click', () => {
        if (sealed) return; load();
        (screen.requestFullscreen?.call(screen) ?? video.webkitEnterFullscreen?.call(video));
      });

      /* drag / click along the nerve */
      const posToTime = x => { const r = nerve.getBoundingClientRect(); return Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (x - r.left) / r.width)) * DURATION; };
      let dragging = false;
      nerve.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => { if (sealed) return; dragging = true; nerve.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); seek(posToTime(e.clientX), !video.paused || !film.dataset.started); });
      nerve.addEventListener('pointermove', e => {
        const s = posToTime(e.clientX); showTip(s, `${fmt(s)} · ${CHAPTERS[chapterAt(s)].t}`);
        if (dragging) seek(s, false);
      });
      nerve.addEventListener('pointerup', () => { dragging = false; });
      nerve.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
        const s = video.currentTime || 0;
        const map = { ArrowRight: s + 5, ArrowLeft: s - 5, Home: 0, End: DURATION - 1, PageDown: CHAPTERS[Math.min(chapterAt(s) + 1, 6)].at, PageUp: CHAPTERS[Math.max(chapterAt(s) - 1, 0)].at };
        if (e.key in map) { e.preventDefault(); seek(map[e.key], !video.paused); }
      });

      /* rail index + per-act "watch from" */
      $$('[data-seek]').forEach(b => b.addEventListener('click', () => {
        seek(+b.dataset.seek, true);
        film.scrollIntoView({ behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth', block: 'center' });
      }));

      /* deep links: /out-loud/automa-chem-2026/#t=3:07 */
      const m = location.hash.match(/t=(\d+):?(\d+)?/);
      if (m && !sealed) { const s = m[2] ? (+m[1] * 60 + +m[2]) : +m[1]; film.dataset.started = '1'; render(s); video.addEventListener('loadedmetadata', () => (video.currentTime = s), { once: true }); load(); }

      render(0);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* rail: title + the six acts, fixed like every other room */
  .acts-index { margin: 3.2rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; width: 13.5rem; }
  .acts-index li { border-top: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.11); }
  .acts-index li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.11); }
  .acts-index button { all: unset; box-sizing: border-box; cursor: pointer; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.9rem 1fr auto; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; width: 100%; padding: 0.55rem 0; }
  .acts-index .n { font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; color: var(--bronze); font-size: 0.82rem; }
  .acts-index .t { font-family: var(--font-display); color: rgba(243, 235, 224, 0.7); font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.2; transition: color 0.5s var(--ease); }
  .acts-index .tc { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.55rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: rgba(230, 203, 155, 0.5); }
  .acts-index button:hover .t, .acts-index button:focus-visible .t { color: var(--bone); }
  .acts-index button:focus-visible { outline: 1.5px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 2px; }
  .acts-index li[data-active="1"] .t { color: var(--gold); }
  .acts-index li[data-active="1"] .n { color: var(--gold); }
  body[data-seal="sealed"] .acts-index .tc { opacity: 0.5; }

  /* room header copy */
  .ol-kicker { letter-spacing: 0.16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--champagne); margin: 0; font-size: 0.66rem; }
  .ol-title { max-width: 16em; font-family: var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0.8rem 0 0; font-size: clamp(2rem, 3vw, 2.7rem); font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--bone); }
  .ol-deck { font-family: var(--font-display); color: var(--flesh); font-style: italic; margin: 0.7rem 0 0; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .ol-lede { font-family: var(--font-display); color: var(--flesh); font-style: italic; max-width: 34rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 0; font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.45; }

  /* ── the film ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .film { margin: 3.2rem 0 0; }
  .screen { position: relative; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: #070707; border: 1px solid rgba(170, 104, 66, 0.33); overflow: hidden; cursor: pointer; }
  .screen video, .screen .poster { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  .screen video { filter: none; }
  .screen .poster { transition: opacity 1.2s var(--ease), filter 1.2s var(--ease); }
  .film[data-started="1"] .poster { opacity: 0; pointer-events: none; }
  .screen:focus-visible { outline: 1.5px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 4px; }

  .now { position: absolute; left: 1rem; bottom: 0.9rem; z-index: 3; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.58rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7); padding: 0.35rem 0.55rem; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.8s var(--ease); }
  .film[data-started="1"] .now { opacity: 1; }

  .cue-play { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 2; display: grid; align-content: start; justify-content: center; justify-items: center; gap: 8px; padding-top: 6.5%; background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,0.78) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.5) 45%, rgba(0,0,0,0.35) 100%); transition: opacity 0.9s var(--ease), background 0.9s var(--ease); }
  .cue-play .cl { width: 1px; height: clamp(18px, 4vw, 40px); background: var(--gold); animation: pulse 5.6s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .cue-play .cd { width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--gold); box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--gold); animation: pulse 5.6s ease-in-out 0.8s infinite; }
